  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a20105d88834d764380d6090e8c10179, type: 3}
  m_Name: A Traveler's Guide to Springtide Meadows
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NoteData
  title: A Traveler's Guide to Springtide Meadows
  content: 'Few places embody the spirit of renewal quite like Springtide Meadows.
    Fed by gentle rivers and blessed with fertile soil, its fields have sustained
    neighboring settlements for generations. During the first bloom of spring, wildflowers
    once spread so far across the plains that travelers likened them to a painted
    sea.


    The people of Springtide are known for their hospitality. It is said
    that no weary traveler leaves the village hungry, so long as there is bread to
    share. Though life follows the rhythm of the harvest, festivals and markets ensure
    the meadows remain lively throughout the year.'
